153: Current delivery addendum: the minimal positive prepared-archive timestamp correction is independently accepted for fresh isolated CI after 129 producer and six independent pure controls; all 126 original test bodies, 1,232 payload entries and 177 product files remain unchanged. Mix 1.20.4 treats a missing target as time zero, so epoch-zero inputs omitted 97 of JOSE's 113 Erlang modules. The prior exact `8888d8e2` network run `40766689512` passed the 895-byte Rebar capture but failed both product methods with `:jose_jwk` unavailable; all three container cleanups passed. Corrected compilation and both product methods remain pending. Source-pair5 now has actual host evidence: 132 Swift Testing SDK tests plus eight XCTest tests, 69 update tests, 31 CLI tests and 30 Python CLI tests passed, including ten source-pair methods. Negative cases use actual rendered children; the positive tool-order sentinel is in process and proves no Android child build. The generated consumer passed four host tests and an iOS simulator-target cross-build with no simulator boot. Engine run `40766689541` still failed the 60-second `context_schema_scalar_reserved_and_lengths` cache-fixture test; five other jobs passed and cleanup completed. Phoenix run `40766689598` passed 697 tests with two skips plus 45 protocol, 24 storage and one migration checks. Architecture run `40768719255` at `dfd0e319` was in progress at the saved 21:05 UTC observation after pure controls and compiler installation; actual full results remain unknown, with two maximum attempts and no retry. FieldLog public `4d17c926` run `40765792113` timed out its `swift-test` command at 480 seconds after pinned SDK resolution, with no observed build completion or test start; failure count is unavailable, all 16 remote groups closed and one SIGTERM was used. Post-test SDK and lock checks were unreached. Its same-pin phase-split diagnostic is under preparation and has not been selected or pushed. The large raw CI review stays local; [published summaries and timestamp selection](verification/github-delivery-positive-timestamp/selection.json) bind its metadata and hashes. Native/UI/capture, disconnected-phone and all local custody/UnitA holds remain; gates stay 8 running, 30 planned, 0 verified.
155: Checkpoint `56ff14c` passes exact binary exports, locked dependency preparation, archive/restore, PostgreSQL isolation and offline compilation in the isolated network lane. It then rejects one fresh 895-byte Rebar `source.dag` after command 89; zero product methods ran, all 107 commands closed and all three owned containers were removed. The exact generated-output classification and opaque 64KiB retention correction passes 126 producer plus six independent pure methods and is selected only for fresh isolated CI. Both second-campaign full attempts are closed: 64M cache work exhausts at 64,000,001 after 41.737 seconds; 128M reaches the original instruction-fuel limit at 100,000,001 after 44.335 seconds. Neither finishes Corpus 1; Corpus 2 remains unrun. All final resources are zero, eleven commands closed and scratch was removed. No replay or default promotion is selected; the prepared Astra algorithm/resource-policy/implementation comparison remains under independent review, with zero runs and no installed workflow. The Swift host job passes 132 SDK tests including all nine axis cases and 69 update tests, then fails its 31 CLI tests with 32 issues from stale compiled source-pair4; later VM/generated-consumer steps were skipped. Reviewed source-pair5 refreshes only two SDK rows and passes eight in-process controls; full CLI/Python validation remains pending. This distribution ID does not authorize the held Android candidate v5. The user authorized public FieldLog publication: repository visibility is verified and one 26-test host run is dispatched at `4062256`, with results pending. The 12-file/38-test adoption draft is source-reviewed but unapplied and unexecuted. All native, custody, UnitA and GA holds remain; gates stay 8 running, 30 planned and 0 verified. Bindings and limits are in [the checkpoint receipt](verification/github-delivery-source-pair-and-rebar/checkpoint.json).
906: 2026-10-28 architecture selection: the corrected two-arm execution comparison passed independent source review (38 supplied pure tests, 412 independent checks, 11 mocked campaigns and 21 prefix cases). Root selected its unchanged finite limits and installed the manual workflow. Both optimized builds, finite/harness checks, actual geometry and cleanup must pass before either full run; at most two full attempts and eleven commands, no retries. Compilation, runtime results, feasibility and production-default promotion remain pending. The previous two-attempt cache campaign stays closed. The new network run at 8888d8e2 reaches both product methods and validates the exact 895-byte Rebar DAG capture, but both methods fail because :jose_jwk is unavailable; prepared archive timestamp correction is under source investigation. The 38-test FieldLog public host run remains pending. Native, device, UI/capture and held-process restrictions remain in force; gates stay 8 running, 30 planned, 0 verified.
